WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:02.336
♪♪

00:00:02.336 --> 00:00:03.337
Hey!

00:00:03.337 --> 00:00:05.339
Oh!
-Ted Lasso welcome-wagon has
arrived!

00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:07.883
(Cheers)

00:00:07.883 --> 00:00:08.884
Ted Lasso.

00:00:08.884 --> 00:00:09.885
Ted Lasso.
Ted Lasso.

00:00:09.885 --> 00:00:10.886
Ted Lasso.
Ted Lasso.

00:00:10.886 --> 00:00:12.888
Ted Lasso is-
-An injection of goodness.

00:00:12.888 --> 00:00:14.181
Woo-hoo! Ugh!

00:00:14.181 --> 00:00:15.182
Oh!
-Ah!

00:00:16.058 --> 00:00:17.059
I'm fine.

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:20.854
The level of thanks that comes
across social media...

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:23.065
Hannah:
Imagine getting tweets
from people saying,

00:00:23.065 --> 00:00:26.068
Hannah:
"We're kinder to each other in
our family because you've

00:00:26.068 --> 00:00:28.195
Hannah:
reminded us that that's what we
should all be."

00:00:28.195 --> 00:00:32.783
It's a choice, isn't it, to be
positive and grateful and I now
find myself saying,

00:00:32.783 --> 00:00:36.954
Brett:
"I appreciate you," to most
people after an interaction.

00:00:36.954 --> 00:00:38.038
This is why it's hard to love
you.

00:00:38.413 --> 00:00:39.414
Oh!

00:00:39.414 --> 00:00:40.415
He loves you!

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:43.627
The positivity that people have
felt about the show and talking
about the kind

00:00:43.627 --> 00:00:48.799
of "Lasso Way," being very funny
but also very human. It's
undeniable.

00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:51.718
Keep an eye on these guys
because around the seventy-four
minute mark,

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.720
there's gonna be a room full of
grown men crying.

00:00:54.388 --> 00:00:55.389
I'll be one of them.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:59.476
Every man and woman is living a
comedy, a drama and a tragedy,

00:00:59.476 --> 00:01:01.478
and the message is reflecting
that notion.

00:01:01.478 --> 00:01:05.190
Speaking with people and the
fans and the reactions changed
my life.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:08.235
Cristo:
I was walking and randomly a
person just starts

00:01:08.235 --> 00:01:09.778
going, "Football is life!
Football is life!"

00:01:09.778 --> 00:01:11.071
Football is life.

00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:15.325
Someone who messaged me on
Twitter said their eleven year
old son missed a shot that

00:01:15.325 --> 00:01:17.494
would've tied the game and she's
like, "Right, I know you're
upset

00:01:17.494 --> 00:01:21.498
but what do we need to do?" And
he goes, "Be a goldfish like
Sam."

00:01:21.498 --> 00:01:24.084
You remember what animal has the
shortest memory?

00:01:24.251 --> 00:01:25.252
A goldfish.

00:01:25.252 --> 00:01:28.714
What do you think we should all
do once we get done being sad?

00:01:29.131 --> 00:01:30.841
I think we should all be a
goldfish.

00:01:31.258 --> 00:01:32.509
I brought you a little
something.
-Oh?

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:33.677
Yeah, cookies.

00:01:34.052 --> 00:01:36.305
Or, as y'all call them here,
biscuits.

00:01:36.555 --> 00:01:39.308
I've been getting a lot of
biscuit recipes. People going,

00:01:39.308 --> 00:01:42.311
"Oh, look at these that we
made," or little videos of them
going, "Oh my God, they

00:01:42.311 --> 00:01:46.481
taste as good as yours!" And who
knew that that whole Biscuits
With The Boss thing

00:01:46.481 --> 00:01:47.482
would go so nuts?

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:50.944
Ted:
I forgive you.

00:01:51.653 --> 00:01:52.654
Why?

00:01:52.988 --> 00:01:56.241
Divorce is hard. It makes folks
do crazy things.

00:01:56.241 --> 00:01:58.702
♪♪

00:01:58.702 --> 00:02:02.331
Jason:
Some of the more profound
responses that have reached me personally have been from people

00:02:02.331 --> 00:02:05.834
going through things that
characters are going through on
the show or just something

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:09.755
that's really taken hope out of
their hearts. And how the show
moved them in a way

00:02:09.755 --> 00:02:11.923
Jason:
that refilled their Love Cup, so
to speak.

00:02:11.923 --> 00:02:13.425
Oh, it feels good to laugh.

00:02:13.842 --> 00:02:15.677
And season two is even better.

00:02:15.677 --> 00:02:19.556
♪♪

00:02:19.556 --> 00:02:22.934
Season two stays as adorable as
the first.

00:02:23.268 --> 00:02:24.269
How long was I out?

00:02:24.269 --> 00:02:25.270
Doesn't matter, you're back now.

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:26.271
Let's do this.

00:02:26.271 --> 00:02:27.272
Ohhh!
(Spits)

00:02:27.272 --> 00:02:28.273
Woo-hoo!

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:32.402
You listen to me, Coach Lasso.
We have work to do.

00:02:32.778 --> 00:02:33.987
Next season.

